## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-cloud, multi-tenant OTCA pipelines with governance and schema contracts.

## Key Concepts

- Federated schema registry with per-tenant Protobuf contracts
- Forward/backward compatibility and versioning
- Tenant isolation via topic scoping and ACLs
- Cross-cloud replication and data deletion/retention governance
- Observability and testing strategies

## Code Example

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";
package otca;
message TelemetryEvent {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string service_id = 2;
  string event_type = 3;
  int64 timestamp = 4;
  int32 latency_ms = 5;
  string model_version = 6;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant deletion across all stores?
- What are trade-offs of Pulsar vs Kafka in a multi-cloud OTCA setup?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes end-to-end streaming design, practical trade-offs in serialization, transport, exactly-once semantics, schema evolution, and testing under production constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Protobuf schemas and Schema Registry
- Kafka transactions and idempotent producers
- Schema evolution compatibility
- Throughput, latency, partitioning, backpressure
- Replay and recovery strategies
- Monitoring and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Producer initialization with transactions
const producer = new Kafka.Producer({ transactionalId: 'telemetry-producer' });
await producer.initTransactions();
await producer.beginTransaction();
try {
  await producer.send({ topic: 'telemetry', messages: [{ key, value }] });
  await producer.commitTransaction();
} catch (e) {
  await producer.abortTransaction();
}
```

